      },
      "date": "2026-10-13 08:20:51.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 5:\n\nPatch Set 5: rebased onto current master. The only conflict was the .TH date line in mkfs.lustre.8.\n\nIt also has the fixes for the Patch Set 4 AI review comments:\n- The power-of-two row warning is now for parity arrays only. raid0 and raid10 do not get it.\n- The mount check now compares the stripe that mballoc really uses: -o stripe=, then stripe_width, then stride.\n- A partition of an md array (for example an LVM PV on md0p1) is now probed.\n- Wording fixes in the comments and in mkfs.lustre.8. mount.lustre.8 now has an entry for stripe=.\n\nCompile-tested only. Not tested on a real md array after these changes.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 5
    },
