        "committer": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-13 08:02:52.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-20564 utils: probe md RAID geometry for OST mkfs/mount",
        "message": "LU-20564 utils: probe md RAID geometry for OST mkfs/mount\n\nmkfs.lustre now probes the md array under an OST target, through any\nstacked dm devices, and seeds -E stride/stripe_width so mballoc can\nalign allocations to full stripes.  mke2fs can derive these from the\nblkid topology, but dm-thin and dm-cache replace optimal_io_size with\ntheir block size when that does not divide the row, and dm-vdo always\nreports 4KiB.  raid0, raid4/5/6, raid10 and raidkm (level 71) are\ndecoded, and user-supplied values are respected.  mount.lustre warns\nwhen an OST on a striped array has no fs geometry, or geometry that\nis not a multiple of the array row, unless it is mounted with\n-o stripe=.\n\nmkfs.lustre also warns about two things that cannot be corrected once\nthe OST is formatted: a partition that does not start on a stripe\nboundary, and, on parity arrays, a data row (k * chunk) that is not\na power of two.  The default bulk RPC sizes are powers of two, so a\nrow that is not one leaves a partial row at the tail of every RPC,\nwhich the array services as a read-modify-write.  mkfs.lustre.8\ngains a RAID ALIGNMENT section covering both, and how to correct\nthem.\n\nTested on RHEL 9.7 against live loop-backed md arrays: raid0/4/5/6,\nraid10 near/far/offset, a non-power-of-two row, user-supplied values,\ndm-linear over one array and spanning two, and misaligned partition\nstarts.  Also tested against live raidkm arrays, plain and\ndeclustered.  In every case the computed row matches md's own\nqueue/optimal_io_size.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:Fable-5 claude-code\nAssisted-by: Claude:Opus-5 claude-code\nChange-Id: I442528cea51a55c6b74f7f2282a1db566eab9783\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
